但凯伦把话题拉了回来，她好像在说，其实我是认真的。

696
00:29:28.400 --> 00:29:32.260
Like, after what happened on the beach, do I have a future with you?
比如，在海滩上的事情发生之后，我和你还有未来吗？

697
00:29:33.140 --> 00:29:36.740
Because I don't feel like I have a future in Scranton, but I'd like to have a future with you.
因为我觉得我在斯克兰顿没有未来，但我希望能和你有未来。

698
00:29:36.880 --> 00:29:40.140
Well, she just says there's one too many people in Scranton.
好吧，她只是说斯克兰顿多了一个不该有的人。

699
00:29:40.140 --> 00:29:40.400
Yeah.
是啊。

700
00:29:40.740 --> 00:29:41.040
You know?
你知道吗？

701
00:29:41.180 --> 00:29:42.560
She was like, I was at the beach.
她当时就说，我在海滩呢。

702
00:29:43.780 --> 00:29:45.080
And I don't know.
然后我也不知道。

703
00:29:45.220 --> 00:29:49.020
He just sort of jokes it off and then grabs her hand and they cross the street.
他就是那种打哈哈敷衍过去，然后拉起她的手过马路。

704
00:29:49.260 --> 00:29:56.660
And I'm sure deep down she knows that he's on the fence.
而且我敢肯定，她内心深处知道他还在犹豫不决。

705
00:29:56.800 --> 00:29:57.920
She's got to know it.
她不可能不知道。

706
00:29:58.340 --> 00:30:00.860
She's trying to practice good self-care.
她正努力好好照顾自己。

707
00:30:01.180 --> 00:30:02.800
She is trying to take care of herself here.
她在这里正努力照顾自己呢。

708
00:30:02.940 --> 00:30:04.040
She's being assertive.
她表现得很坚决。

709
00:30:04.040 --> 00:30:09.920
But then she's not really reading the signals, which I think are super clear.
但她并没有真正捕捉到那些信号，我觉得那些信号已经超级明显了。

710
00:30:10.720 --> 00:30:13.260
You don't ever read them when you don't want to see them, though.
不过，当你不想看到的时候，你是永远都不会去注意它们的。

711
00:30:13.680 --> 00:30:14.420
That's true.
没错。

712
00:30:14.540 --> 00:30:16.080
Put that on a t-shirt.
这话应该印在T恤上。

713
00:30:17.320 --> 00:30:17.920
All right.
好了。

714
00:30:18.020 --> 00:30:21.740
So now it's the next morning and it's interview time.
所以现在是第二天早上，采访时间到了。

715
00:30:21.980 --> 00:30:24.220
Karen, Jim, and Michael are waiting in the lobby.
凯伦、吉姆和迈克尔正在大厅里等候。

716
00:30:24.640 --> 00:30:30.200
I should own the fact, since I was snarky about the lobby just having a bunch of brown sticks,
我得承认，既然我之前对大厅里只有一堆棕色树枝冷嘲热讽过，

717
00:30:30.240 --> 00:30:33.340
that there is also a big plant on the other side of it.
那我也得承认大厅另一边其实还有一株大植物。

718
00:30:33.340 --> 00:30:34.960
A big potted plant, everyone.
一盆大植物，各位。

719
00:30:35.200 --> 00:30:37.360
A little bit of green in the corner.
角落里的一点绿意。

720
00:30:38.300 --> 00:30:39.460
There you go.
这不就有了嘛。

721
00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:41.500
Well, that is nice.
好吧，那确实挺不错的。

722
00:30:41.740 --> 00:30:42.300
It is nice.
确实挺不错的。

723
00:30:42.300 --> 00:30:42.600
That's nice.
挺不错的。

724
00:30:42.820 --> 00:30:47.160
And I'm sorry I was so snarky about your big brown sticks.
而且我很抱歉之前对你们那些大棕色树枝冷嘲热讽。

725
00:30:48.040 --> 00:30:56.220
Well, back at Dunder Mifflin, Dwight has appointed Andy as his number two officially.
好了，镜头回到邓德·米夫林，德怀特正式任命安迪为他的哼哈二将。

726
00:30:56.700 --> 00:30:58.460
And Andy has accepted.
安迪也接受了。

727
00:30:58.760 --> 00:31:02.600
And Jenna, we do that really cool thing, except now it's Dwight,
珍娜，我们拍了那个超级酷的镜头，只不过主角换成了德怀特，

728
00:31:02.600 --> 00:31:05.220
where we start on him and we reveal Andy in the corner.
我们先拍他，然后镜头摇过去露出角落里的安迪。

729
00:31:06.160 --> 00:31:06.600
Yes.
对。

730
00:31:06.900 --> 00:31:08.500
You know that's my favorite thing.
你知道那是我的最爱。

731
00:31:08.700 --> 00:31:08.820
I know.
我知道。

732
00:31:09.040 --> 00:31:09.440
I know.
我知道。

733
00:31:09.880 --> 00:31:14.260
Andy has this talking head and it's at 21 minutes, 54 seconds.
安迪有个单人访谈镜头，在21分54秒处。

734
00:31:14.460 --> 00:31:17.580
He's saying, you know, three months ago I was a Cornell grad in anger management,
他说，你知道的，三个月前我还是个康奈尔大学毕业生，还在上情绪管理课，

735
00:31:17.580 --> 00:31:18.600
but look at me now.
但看看现在的我。

736
00:31:18.760 --> 00:31:20.860
And he's washing out, you know, Dwight's mug.
当时他正在洗，你知道的，德怀特的马克杯。

737
00:31:21.560 --> 00:31:23.060
Jenna, can you hear that sink?
珍娜，你能听到那个水槽的声音吗？

738
00:31:23.060 --> 00:31:28.340
I couldn't not laugh because you and I know it's a fake sink.
我忍不住笑了，因为你我都知那是个假水槽。

739
00:31:28.360 --> 00:31:33.060
And it had that weird tinny sound because the water was going underneath into a bucket.
而且它有一种奇怪的金属回音，因为水是流到底下的一个桶里的。

740
00:31:33.640 --> 00:31:33.960
Yes.
对。

741
00:31:34.120 --> 00:31:38.180
They had a little pump that would pump water through that faucet,
他们有个小泵可以把水抽到水龙头里，

742
00:31:38.320 --> 00:31:41.960
but then it just came down the drain into a bucket.
但水顺着下水道流下来直接进了一个桶。

743
00:31:42.220 --> 00:31:42.400
Yeah.
对啊。

744
00:31:42.660 --> 00:31:43.780
There's no plumbing there.
那里根本没有管道。

745
00:31:44.540 --> 00:31:45.260
There's no plumbing.
根本没有管道。

746
00:31:45.560 --> 00:31:46.220
That's right.
没错。

747
00:31:46.440 --> 00:31:48.040
They would set it up and take it away.
他们每次拍完就会把它安好然后拆走。

748
00:31:48.040 --> 00:31:53.860
So something you could not do is improvise turning on the sink because nothing would come out.
所以有一件事你是绝对不能做的，那就是即兴表演去开水龙头，因为什么都不会流出来。

749
00:31:54.320 --> 00:31:57.360
Or pour anything down the drain because it would just hit the ground.
或者把什么东西倒进下水道里，因为那会直接洒到地上。

750
00:31:57.920 --> 00:31:58.360
Correct.
没错。

751
00:31:58.800 --> 00:31:59.260
Correct.
没错。

752
00:32:00.040 --> 00:32:05.260
Well, now we have the scene where Dwight pulls Pam aside.
好了，现在我们来到德怀特把帕姆拉到一旁的这场戏。

753
00:32:06.200 --> 00:32:08.960
He explains he's very impressed by her coal walk.
他解释说他非常佩服她走炭火的表现。

754
00:32:09.820 --> 00:32:15.740
And he would like her to be his secret assistant to the regional manager.
他希望她能担任他秘密的地区经理助理。

755
00:32:16.160 --> 00:32:17.440
And she accepts.
然后她接受了。

756
00:32:17.820 --> 00:32:19.520
Everything about the scene was delightful.
这场戏的方方面面都太美妙了。

757
00:32:19.820 --> 00:32:21.360
I loved every single thing about it.
我喜欢里面的每一处细节。

758
00:32:21.480 --> 00:32:22.780
I love Dwight's bravado.
我喜欢德怀特的虚张声势。

759
00:32:23.040 --> 00:32:27.100
And Pam's just like, uh-huh, uh-huh.
而帕姆就好像是，嗯哼，嗯哼。

760
00:32:27.240 --> 00:32:29.460
Like, what an idiot, but I'm going to go along with it.
就像是，真是个笨蛋，不过我倒要看看他想搞什么鬼。

761
00:32:30.220 --> 00:32:33.300
Well, I think this is her way of staying connected to Jim.
嗯，我觉得这是她与吉姆保持联系的一种方式。

762
00:32:33.540 --> 00:32:38.160
He's all the way in New York, but she has this talking head where she says she learned from Jim
他远在纽约，但她有一段画外音说她从吉姆那里学到了

763
00:32:38.160 --> 00:32:44.540
If Dwight ever asks you to accept something in secret, you reply, absolutely I do.
如果德怀特要求你秘密接受什么事，你就回答，我当然愿意。

764
00:32:44.760 --> 00:32:50.180
So I think throughout this whole episode when Pam is doing this little bit with Dwight,
所以我觉得在这一整集里，当帕姆和德怀特玩这个小把戏时，

765
00:32:50.400 --> 00:32:54.620
she is imagining how she's going to get to tell Jim all about it.
她一直在幻想着自己要怎么把这一切都讲给吉姆听。

766
00:32:54.780 --> 00:32:55.940
Oh, for sure.
哦，绝对是这样。

767
00:32:56.140 --> 00:32:56.880
For sure.
肯定的。

768
00:32:57.380 --> 00:33:00.380
Well, here is Dwight's team as he sees it.
好了，这是德怀特眼中的团队阵容。

769
00:33:00.680 --> 00:33:02.620
Dwight is the regional manager.
德怀特是地区经理。

770
00:33:02.960 --> 00:33:05.560
Dwight is also the assistant regional manager.
德怀特同时也是助理地区经理。

771
00:33:05.560 --> 00:33:08.280
Andy is his number two because it's political.
安迪是他的二把手，因为这是出于政治考量。

772
00:33:09.080 --> 00:33:11.820
Pam is the secret assistant to their regional manager.
帕姆是他们地区经理的秘密助理。

773
00:33:12.060 --> 00:33:13.040
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

774
00:33:13.280 --> 00:33:19.620
In a deleted scene, we find out that Angela is the spy in charge of the secret assistant
在一个被删减的片段中，我们发现安吉拉才是负责监视地区经理

775
00:33:19.620 --> 00:33:20.660
to their regional manager.
秘密助理的间谍。

776
00:33:21.360 --> 00:33:23.020
Oh, and what does that mean?
哦，那是什么意思？

777
00:33:23.320 --> 00:33:30.240
Well, as soon as Pam says, yeah, absolutely I do, and agrees to be the secret assistant to
嗯，就在帕姆说，行，我当然愿意，并同意成为地区经理的秘密助理之后，

778
00:33:30.240 --> 00:33:34.120
the regional manager, she leaves, and when she does, the scene plays out.
她离开了，紧接着这一幕就上演了。

779
00:33:34.540 --> 00:33:37.640
Dwight calls Angela and says, keep an eye on Pam.
德怀特打电话给安吉拉说，盯紧帕姆。

780
00:33:38.060 --> 00:33:39.600
And Angela's like, done.
安吉拉就说，交给我。

781
00:33:39.820 --> 00:33:45.500
And then immediately, my little head pops over the partition between accounting and reception,
然后紧接着，我的小脑袋就从会计部和前台之间的隔板探了出来，

782
00:33:45.500 --> 00:33:47.340
