然后我就开始监视你。

783
00:33:47.980 --> 00:33:48.900
Oh, that's amazing.
哦，太棒了。

784
00:33:48.900 --> 00:33:49.640
I'm watching you.
我盯着你呢。

785
00:33:49.700 --> 00:33:50.460
I'm watching you.
我正看着你呢。

786
00:33:50.660 --> 00:33:52.640
Oh, I wish they'd left that in.
哦，真希望他们把这段保留下来。

787
00:33:52.880 --> 00:33:53.200
I know.
我也这么觉得。

788
00:33:53.280 --> 00:33:54.500
It's a fun detail, right?
是个有趣的细节，对吧？

789
00:33:54.500 --> 00:33:56.360
I love that detail.
我太喜欢这个细节了。

790
00:33:56.980 --> 00:34:02.180
Well, now, lady, we go back to corporate, and Michael's interview has begun.
好了，女士，现在我们回到总公司，迈克的面试开始了。

791
00:34:03.080 --> 00:34:05.940
Andy Buckley is so fantastic in this scene.
安迪·巴克利在这场戏里太棒了。

792
00:34:06.120 --> 00:34:10.760
I mean, Steve is always fantastic, but to watch Steve as Michael, because Michael's so
我是说，史蒂夫一直都很棒，但是看着史蒂夫饰演的迈克，因为迈克太荒谬了，

793
00:34:10.760 --> 00:34:18.800
ridiculous, play off someone who's so believably a corporate person, it just was so fun to watch.
去和这样一个极具真实感的公司高管飙戏，看着实在是太有趣了。

794
00:34:18.800 --> 00:34:25.820
So my favorite part of this scene with David and Michael is when he asks Michael where he sees
所以我和大卫以及迈克这场戏中最喜欢的部分，就是他问迈克觉得哪里

795
00:34:25.820 --> 00:34:26.840
room for improvement.
还有改进的空间。

796
00:34:28.280 --> 00:34:32.720
And Michael's suggestion is that they rename the company altogether.
而迈克的建议是他们干脆把公司名字给改了。

797
00:34:33.500 --> 00:34:35.680
You know his three names, right?
你知道他的三个名字吧？

798
00:34:35.780 --> 00:34:36.640
His three suggestions?
他的三个建议？

799
00:34:36.960 --> 00:34:38.020
I wrote them down.
我都记下来了。

800
00:34:38.200 --> 00:34:38.320
Yeah.
对。

801
00:34:39.400 --> 00:34:40.580
Here are the names.
名字都在这。

802
00:34:41.080 --> 00:34:41.940
Paper Great.
伟大纸业。

803
00:34:42.880 --> 00:34:44.600
Great Papers Our Passion.
伟大纸业，我们倾注热情。

804
00:34:45.300 --> 00:34:46.660
We're Great.
我们很伟大。

805
00:34:47.320 --> 00:34:48.520
Super Duper Paper.
超级无敌纸业。

806
00:34:48.800 --> 00:34:50.180
Or just Super Duper.
或者就叫超级无敌。

807
00:34:50.420 --> 00:34:50.740
Yeah.
对。

808
00:34:51.180 --> 00:34:52.060
Any of those.
这些都可以。

809
00:34:52.180 --> 00:34:53.120
Any of those could work.
这些名字哪个都行。

810
00:34:53.900 --> 00:34:56.200
Well, we had a fan question from Rebecca W.
对了，我们收到了丽贝卡·W的粉丝提问。

811
00:34:56.240 --> 00:35:01.860
She said, were the suggestions Michael gave for a change of name of the company improvised?
她说，迈克尔之前提议的公司改名方案是即兴发挥的吗？

812
00:35:02.220 --> 00:35:03.700
I checked the script.
我查过剧本了。

813
00:35:03.980 --> 00:35:08.840
They were all in there with the exception of Super Duper Paper and Super Duper.
除了“超级无敌纸业”和“超级无敌”，其他的剧本里都有。

814
00:35:10.180 --> 00:35:11.040
Those were.
那两个是即兴的。

815
00:35:11.900 --> 00:35:16.200
But there was also way more to this interview scene.
但这场采访戏其实还有更多内容。

816
00:35:16.200 --> 00:35:19.460
And I have to ask you, Angela, are they in the deleted scenes?
安吉拉，我得问问你，这些被删减的片段里有吗？

817
00:35:19.460 --> 00:35:21.400
Because they were so funny.
因为它们太搞笑了。

818
00:35:21.660 --> 00:35:25.540
There are so many deleted scenes for this particular episode.
这一集有超多被删减的片段。

819
00:35:25.540 --> 00:35:29.060
And this scene has several and they are hilarious.
这场戏删了好几段，而且都笑死人了。

820
00:35:29.400 --> 00:35:34.680
One of my favorite ones is that David says, what do you see in the future?
我最喜欢的片段之一是大卫问：你对未来有什么看法？

821
00:35:35.040 --> 00:35:37.060
You know, but he's meaning about the company.
你知道的，他是指公司的事。

822
00:35:37.260 --> 00:35:39.380
You know, where do you see the future going here?
你知道，你觉得这里的未来会怎样？

823
00:35:39.860 --> 00:35:42.840
And Michael goes, he goes on about all this stuff.
然后迈克尔就开始滔滔不绝地说各种事。

824
00:35:43.180 --> 00:35:46.120
He goes on about how many kids he's going to have and all this stuff.
他大谈自己以后会有多少个孩子之类的。

825
00:35:46.220 --> 00:35:56.340
But then he says, also, I think there could be one vitamin that you take for all of these other vitamins.
但接着他又说，他还觉得可以有一种能替代其他所有维生素的综合维生素。

826
00:35:56.340 --> 00:35:57.660
But it's just one.
但就只要吃一颗。

827
00:35:57.860 --> 00:35:58.500
I don't know.
我不知道。

828
00:35:59.120 --> 00:36:03.200
And David Wallace goes, you mean a multivitamin?
大卫·华莱士就说：你是说多维片吗？

829
00:36:03.900 --> 00:36:06.020
And Michael's like, I don't know what they're going to call it.
迈克尔就说：我不知道他们会给它起名叫什么。

830
00:36:06.140 --> 00:36:06.980
Like, I don't know.
就，我不知道。

831
00:36:07.660 --> 00:36:08.060
Yes.
对。

832
00:36:08.060 --> 00:36:09.300
It is so funny.
真的太好笑了。

833
00:36:09.440 --> 00:36:11.820
But there are great deleted scenes for this episode.
不过这一集有很多超棒的删减片段。

834
00:36:12.580 --> 00:36:16.200
That multivitamin thing was in the script and it made me laugh out loud when I read it.
那个多维片的梗剧本里就有，我读的时候直接笑出声了。

835
00:36:16.300 --> 00:36:17.200
It is hilarious.
太爆笑了。

836
00:36:17.220 --> 00:36:19.700
When he's like, I don't know what they're going to call it.
当他说“我不知道他们会给它起名叫什么”的时候。

837
00:36:19.860 --> 00:36:21.040
But that's the idea.
但创意就是这样。

838
00:36:21.040 --> 00:36:25.880
And David Wallace's look to him is just like, OK.
大卫·华莱士看着他的眼神就像是在说，好吧。

839
00:36:26.180 --> 00:36:28.280
And he's like, thanks for coming in, Michael.
然后他说，谢谢你来面试，迈克尔。

840
00:36:29.160 --> 00:36:32.180
So, you know, Michael feels like he's had a pretty great interview.
所以，你懂的，迈克尔觉得自己这次面试表现相当不错。

841
00:36:32.380 --> 00:36:33.260
He's on his way out.
他正要离开。

842
00:36:33.380 --> 00:36:36.580
And he says, oh, you should know that Jan and I are dating again.
然后他说，哦，你得知道简和我又复合了。

843
00:36:36.580 --> 00:36:39.120
So I'm going to need to fill out one of those love documents.
所以我得去填一份那种恋爱关系文件。

844
00:36:40.200 --> 00:36:47.800
And David Wallace is like, well, you should know that this job you're interviewing for is to replace Jan.
而大卫·华莱士的反应是，好吧，你得知道你来应征的这个职位是要取代简的。

845
00:36:48.300 --> 00:36:53.440
And Jenna, all I could think of was like, no, you can't tell Michael this kind of information.
珍娜，我当时满脑子都在想，不，你不能把这种消息告诉迈克尔。

846
00:36:53.700 --> 00:36:56.780
There is no way this man can hold on to that.
这男人根本藏不住话。

847
00:36:56.960 --> 00:37:02.580
You know what it made me think of Angela is when he says I need to sign another one of those love documents.
安吉拉，你知道这让我想到什么吗，就是他说需要再签一份那种恋爱关系文件的时候。

848
00:37:02.820 --> 00:37:12.580
I was like, it reminded me in Dinner Party when Michael explains he's had a vasectomy, but then had it reversed and then had a vasectomy and then had it reversed.
我当时就觉得，这让我想起《晚宴》那一集里，迈克尔解释说他做了输精管切除手术，然后又做复通手术，接着又做了切除，然后又做了复通。

849
00:37:12.980 --> 00:37:16.100
I was like, how many of these documents have they been signing?
我在想，他们到底签了多少次这种文件啊？

850
00:37:16.600 --> 00:37:17.900
It's like, we're on, we're off.
感觉就像，分分合合没完没了。

851
00:37:18.020 --> 00:37:18.880
We're on, we're off.
时好时坏。

852
00:37:19.040 --> 00:37:23.180
And I wonder also if they had dramatic ripping in half of the document.
我也在想，他们当时有没有戏剧性地把文件撕成两半。

853
00:37:23.640 --> 00:37:24.080
Yes.
没错。

854
00:37:24.420 --> 00:37:27.160
I have so many questions about the love document.
我对这份“爱情文件”有太多的疑问了。

855
00:37:27.160 --> 00:37:28.560
But I agree with you.
但我同意你的看法。

856
00:37:29.620 --> 00:37:37.200
This news to Michael that the job he's applying for is Jan's job and she doesn't know yet that she's going to be let go.
迈克尔应聘的这个职位其实是简的，而简现在还不知道自己要被炒鱿鱼了，这个消息对迈克尔来说……

857
00:37:37.420 --> 00:37:41.160
This is a secret that you should not allow Michael to hold.
这是一个绝不能让迈克尔知道的秘密。

858
00:37:41.360 --> 00:37:43.500
You can't tell Michael any secret.
你什么秘密都不能告诉迈克尔。

859
00:37:43.500 --> 00:37:49.000
You couldn't say, hey, don't tell anyone, but I have toe fungus.
你不能说，嘿，别告诉别人，但我有脚气。

860
00:37:49.420 --> 00:37:50.080
Forget it.
算了吧。

861
00:37:50.500 --> 00:37:56.660
The next thing out of his mouth would be, I'm so sorry you have toe fungus in front of everyone.
他嘴里蹦出来的下一句话就会是，当着所有人的面说，我很遗憾你得了脚气。

862
00:37:57.120 --> 00:37:57.640
Yes.
对。

863
00:37:57.640 --> 00:37:59.040
I don't have toe fungus.
我没有得脚气。

864
00:37:59.220 --> 00:38:00.420
I was just trying to think of something.
我只是随便举个例子。

865
00:38:00.680 --> 00:38:02.600
I have fungus on my toenails.
我的脚趾甲确实有真菌感染。

866
00:38:02.820 --> 00:38:04.980
I know, but you treated it and it's all better.
我知道，但你治疗过，已经全好了。

867
00:38:05.720 --> 00:38:06.880
It came back.
又复发了。

868
00:38:07.080 --> 00:38:07.760
It did?
是吗？

869
00:38:08.340 --> 00:38:08.780
Yeah.
对啊。

870
00:38:09.260 --> 00:38:17.640
You know, if you wear nail polish long enough and your toenails don't get a good amount of oxygen, you can get in.
你知道的，如果你涂指甲油的时间太久，脚趾甲呼吸不到足够的氧气，就会中招。

871
00:38:17.780 --> 00:38:22.300
You know, it's by the way, everyone toe fungus is just like on your toenail.
顺便告诉大家，脚气其实就长在你的脚趾甲上。

872
00:38:22.460 --> 00:38:24.120
It's just like a little white spot.
就像一个小小白点。

873
00:38:24.500 --> 00:38:24.640
Yeah.
对。

874
00:38:25.160 --> 00:38:26.620
That's what those white spots are.
那些白点就是这么回事。

875
00:38:26.760 --> 00:38:26.940
Everyone.
各位。

876
00:38:26.960 --> 00:38:29.140
If you're like, what are these white spots on my toenails?
如果你在想，我脚趾甲上的这些白点是什么？

877
00:38:29.140 --> 00:38:31.820
When I take off my nail polish, that's toe fungus, y'all.
当我卸掉指甲油时，那就是脚气，各位。

878
00:38:31.980 --> 00:38:37.120
And you can get a special like oil and polish to put on there to get rid of it if you care.
如果你介意的话，你可以买一种特殊的精油和指甲油抹在上面来消除它。

879
00:38:37.440 --> 00:38:42.200
Well, my mom always would say every once in a while, just take your toenail polish off and let your toenails breathe.
嗯，我妈以前总会时不时地说，把指甲油卸掉，让脚趾甲透透气。

880
00:38:42.460 --> 00:38:43.340
It's good advice.
这是个好建议。

881
00:38:43.680 --> 00:38:44.460
It's not pretty.
不过不好看。

882
00:38:44.700 --> 00:38:47.100
You're going to have a week of like funky looking yellow toes.
你会有整整一个星期顶着难看的黄脚趾。

883
00:38:47.420 --> 00:38:47.660
Sorry.
抱歉。

884
00:38:49.540 --> 00:38:50.000
All right.
好吧。

885
00:38:50.120 --> 00:38:50.780
Sorry, sorry, sorry.
对不起，对不起，对不起。

886
00:38:50.860 --> 00:38:51.500
Where are we?
我们讲到哪了？

887
00:38:51.720 --> 00:38:56.020
Well, we need to go back to Dunder Mifflin because Dwight would like everyone to gather in the conference room.
嗯，我们得回到邓德米夫林，因为德怀特想让大家在会议室集合。

888
00:38:56.020 --> 00:39:01.780
He needs to discuss and introduce the Schroetbuck reward system.
他需要讨论并介绍“薛特巴克”奖励系统。

889
00:39:04.590 --> 00:39:06.070
It was so funny to me.
我觉得这太搞笑了。

890
00:39:06.250 --> 00:39:07.670
You know what I loved about this?
你知道我最喜欢这个地方的什么吗？

891
00:39:07.830 --> 00:39:11.570
First of all, at 25 minutes, three seconds, Angela's so proud.
首先，在二十五分零三秒的时候，安吉拉太骄傲了。

892
00:39:11.950 --> 00:39:13.090
She's so proud.
她太自豪了。

893
00:39:13.490 --> 00:39:14.570
She has this look.
她露出了那种神情。

894
00:39:14.810 --> 00:39:17.210
Dwight is calling his first conference room meeting.
德怀特正在召开他的第一次会议室会议。

895
00:39:17.210 --> 00:39:18.910
She can't believe it.
她简直不敢相信。

896
00:39:19.050 --> 00:39:21.210
But I love how he leads everyone in.
但我喜欢他是怎么把大家都带进去的。

897
00:39:21.330 --> 00:39:23.370
He's like, no more meetings, right?
他说，再也没有会议了，对吧？

898
00:39:23.510 --> 00:39:25.370
Michael had all these useless meetings.
迈克尔开了那么多无用的会。

899
00:39:25.850 --> 00:39:27.510
Instead, we're going to have lectures.
相反，我们要上课。

900
00:39:29.050 --> 00:39:29.490
Yes.
没错。

901
00:39:30.110 --> 00:39:31.750
And Pam can't wait.
而且帕姆已经等不及了。

902
00:39:31.970 --> 00:39:32.930
She's like, what is he going to do?
她就像是在说，他到底要干什么？

903
00:39:32.990 --> 00:39:33.550
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

904
00:39:33.650 --> 00:39:34.890
I can't wait to see what's about to happen.
我等不及想看看接下来会发生什么。

905
00:39:35.170 --> 00:39:38.470
Well, we get in there and we start getting our first lecture.
好吧，我们进去了，然后开始听我们的第一堂课。

906
00:39:39.390 --> 00:39:43.870
And it is about the origin of paper making.
内容是关于造纸术的起源。

907
00:39:44.110 --> 00:39:44.230
Yeah.
是啊。

908
00:39:44.430 --> 00:39:49.870
He starts with a bunch of Tupperware tins full of soil, different types of soil.
他拿出一堆装满土的特百惠盒子，各种不同的土。

909
00:39:49.870 --> 00:39:56.670
And he asked the question, what would you say is the most important element in the production
他提出了一个问题，你们觉得在生产

910
00:39:56.670 --> 00:39:58.690
of above ground leafy growth?
地上枝叶生长过程中，最重要的元素是什么？

911
00:39:59.930 --> 00:40:02.070
You probably think it's phosphorus.
你们可能会觉得是磷。

912
00:40:02.070 --> 00:40:05.190
And then Angela secretly shakes her head no.
然后安吉拉偷偷摇头说不是。

913
00:40:05.370 --> 00:40:06.790
I improvised that.
那是我即兴发挥的。

914
00:40:06.790 --> 00:40:09.950
And our camera operator caught it and was like, oh, that's so good.
我们的摄影师拍到了，然后就觉得，哦，太棒了。

915
00:40:10.130 --> 00:40:10.950
Ken loved it.
肯很喜欢。

916
00:40:11.050 --> 00:40:12.550
And he told me to keep doing it.
他让我继续这么做。

917
00:40:13.110 --> 00:40:14.050
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

918
00:40:14.050 --> 00:40:17.690
Like, I obviously knew this speech that Dwight had practiced it for me.
就像，我显然知道德怀特为我练习过这段台词。

919
00:40:17.830 --> 00:40:19.370
I used to love having those moments.
我以前很喜欢那种时刻。

920
00:40:19.730 --> 00:40:22.130
I'm sure he practiced it for you.
我敢肯定他为你排练过。

921
00:40:22.130 --> 00:40:22.370
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

922
00:40:22.370 --> 00:40:23.630
And he's killing it.
而且他讲得太棒了。

923
00:40:23.850 --> 00:40:26.530
According to you, you're like, he's killing it.
照你这么说，你就像是在说，他讲得太棒了。

924
00:40:26.870 --> 00:40:27.790
Crushing it.
帅呆了。

925
00:40:27.790 --> 00:40:32.190
By the way, the answer is nitrogen, per Dwight.
顺便说一句，根据德怀特的说法，答案是氮。

926
00:40:32.910 --> 00:40:34.590
Lady, I had to know.
拜托，我必须得知道。

927
00:40:34.830 --> 00:40:35.810
Did you look it up?
你查过了吗？

928
00:40:35.890 --> 00:40:37.010
Did you look up phosphorus?
你查过磷了吗？

929
00:40:37.890 --> 00:40:40.170
You know that website Quora?
你知道Quora那个网站吗？

930
00:40:40.710 --> 00:40:40.830
Yeah.
知道。

931
00:40:40.990 --> 00:40:45.890
It's where you post a question about something and then experts on that subject weigh in.
就是你在上面发布一个关于某事的问题，然后该领域的专家会发表意见。

932
00:40:46.030 --> 00:40:47.250
Did you post the question?
你发问题了吗？

933
00:40:47.990 --> 00:40:49.610
I didn't post the question.
我没发问题。

934
00:40:49.610 --> 00:40:50.670
Oh, I got real excited.
哦，我当时可兴奋了。

935
00:40:51.110 --> 00:40:55.330
But years ago, someone posted that exact question.
但几年前，有人发布了那个一模一样的问题。

936
00:40:55.330 --> 00:40:57.010
The wording was exact.
措辞一模一样。

937
00:40:57.890 --> 00:40:59.630
Exactly what Dwight says.
跟德怀特说的一字不差。

938
00:40:59.790 --> 00:41:03.430
There was an office fan years ago that was like, wait, is this true?
几年前有个《办公室》的粉丝觉得，等等，这是真的吗？

939
00:41:03.670 --> 00:41:12.330
So it's really amazing the back and forth from all the people who are not realizing that this is a direct quote from an office episode.
所以真的很有趣，那些没有意识到这直接出自《办公室》某集台词的人们在来回讨论。

940
00:41:12.330 --> 00:41:16.870
It is just soil scientists weighing in.
