00:48:21.190 --> 00:48:23.770
They've got their golfing and their shooting of the hoops.
他们有高尔夫球和投篮。

1099
00:48:23.970 --> 00:48:26.210
And, you know, yeah.
而且，你知道，对吧。

1100
00:48:26.530 --> 00:48:29.010
Well, while this is going on, these interviews.
嗯，在这一切发生的同时，还有这些面试。

1101
00:48:29.290 --> 00:48:31.810
I just said I was sorry to get out my soapbox.
我刚刚说我很抱歉，免得又开始长篇大论了。

1102
00:48:31.970 --> 00:48:32.750
Oh, my God.
噢，天哪。

1103
00:48:32.750 --> 00:48:33.730
I did it again.
我又犯了。

1104
00:48:33.970 --> 00:48:35.010
I just apologized.
我刚刚道歉了。

1105
00:48:36.130 --> 00:48:37.570
I can't stop it.
我停不下来。

1106
00:48:37.690 --> 00:48:38.730
We can't stop it.
我们停不下来。

1107
00:48:38.870 --> 00:48:39.770
We will stop.
我们会停的。

1108
00:48:40.310 --> 00:48:41.130
We'll try.
我们会试试的。

1109
00:48:41.490 --> 00:48:41.890
We'll try.
我们会试试的。

1110
00:48:42.470 --> 00:48:42.750
Okay.
好吧。

1111
00:48:42.930 --> 00:48:43.390
So, listen.
那么，听着。

1112
00:48:43.650 --> 00:48:48.390
While Karen is interviewing, Michael goes to Jan's office.
当凯伦在面试时，迈克尔去了简的办公室。

1113
00:48:49.070 --> 00:48:49.530
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

1114
00:48:49.910 --> 00:48:50.370
Nope.
不对。

1115
00:48:50.690 --> 00:48:50.950
Nope.
不对。

1116
00:48:50.950 --> 00:48:52.310
He should have just kept on walking.
他本该直接走过去的。

1117
00:48:53.550 --> 00:48:58.630
He immediately tells her that she's going to be fired.
他立刻告诉她她要被解雇了。

1118
00:48:58.810 --> 00:48:59.910
She's being replaced.
她要被取代了。

1119
00:49:00.510 --> 00:49:06.770
So, of course, Jan storms in to Karen's interview and starts yelling at him.
所以，理所当然地，简气势汹汹地闯进凯伦的面试，开始冲他大吼大叫。

1120
00:49:06.930 --> 00:49:09.370
She says, hey, you son of a bitch.
她说，嘿，你这个混蛋。

1121
00:49:09.870 --> 00:49:11.850
Like, just right away.
就像是，马上就开始了。

1122
00:49:13.010 --> 00:49:14.810
And David is so calm.
而大卫是如此镇定。

1123
00:49:14.810 --> 00:49:21.010
We talked about this last week with Paul, where Paul really admired David for being so pointed
我们上周跟保罗讨论过这个，保罗真的很佩服大卫在这种时刻表现得那么针锋相对

1124
00:49:21.010 --> 00:49:22.810
and calm during this moment.
又镇定自若。

1125
00:49:22.810 --> 00:49:26.770
And he says, Jan, this is long overdue.
然后他说，简，这早就该发生了。

1126
00:49:27.090 --> 00:49:28.110
Long overdue.
早就该发生了。

1127
00:49:28.230 --> 00:49:30.330
You've shown no interest in your job lately.
你最近对工作表现得毫无兴趣。

1128
00:49:31.530 --> 00:49:33.670
We can never get a hold of you.
我们根本联系不上你。

1129
00:49:33.950 --> 00:49:35.730
Very erratic behavior.
行为非常古怪。

1130
00:49:36.110 --> 00:49:37.810
Like, your head's not here.
就像，你的心思不在这里。

1131
00:49:38.010 --> 00:49:39.150
You're not here.
你根本不在状态。

1132
00:49:39.810 --> 00:49:41.570
He calls her unstable.
他称她情绪不稳定。

1133
00:49:41.570 --> 00:49:41.670
Unstable.
不稳定。

1134
00:49:42.070 --> 00:49:42.190
Yeah.
是啊。

1135
00:49:42.750 --> 00:49:44.710
And then Michael's like, you're unstable.
然后迈克尔来了一句，你才不稳定。

1136
00:49:45.090 --> 00:49:47.630
And then David's like, I'm sorry, what?
然后大卫说，不好意思，什么？

1137
00:49:47.810 --> 00:49:48.650
And Michael's like, never mind.
然后迈克尔说，没事。

1138
00:49:48.750 --> 00:49:49.330
We're all unstable.
我们大家都不稳定。

1139
00:49:49.530 --> 00:49:49.970
What's happening?
这都在搞什么？

1140
00:49:51.370 --> 00:49:53.910
Michael also insists he didn't tell her.
迈克尔还坚称不是他告诉她的。

1141
00:49:54.050 --> 00:49:54.310
Yeah.
是啊。

1142
00:49:54.890 --> 00:49:55.610
It wasn't me.
不是我。

1143
00:49:55.770 --> 00:49:57.550
While hiding behind the partition.
同时躲在隔断后面。

1144
00:49:57.890 --> 00:49:59.230
I didn't say anything.
我什么都没说。

1145
00:50:00.550 --> 00:50:03.790
Well, Jan asks if this is because of her new boobs.
好吧，简问这是否是因为她做了新胸部。

1146
00:50:04.010 --> 00:50:05.330
Because Michael loves them.
因为迈克尔很喜欢。

1147
00:50:05.530 --> 00:50:06.670
And she doesn't care.
而她根本不在乎。

1148
00:50:07.590 --> 00:50:08.110
Yeah.
是啊。

1149
00:50:08.410 --> 00:50:09.090
He loves them.
他很喜欢。

1150
00:50:09.190 --> 00:50:10.830
That's all that matters to her.
对她来说这就够了。

1151
00:50:10.830 --> 00:50:13.870
Well, then she's being escorted out of the office.
好吧，然后她就被护送出了办公室。

1152
00:50:13.990 --> 00:50:15.590
She's got a bunch of stuff.
她拿了一大堆东西。

1153
00:50:16.050 --> 00:50:17.390
She hugs Hunter.
她拥抱了亨特。

1154
00:50:17.790 --> 00:50:20.710
Her whole scene with Hunter is brilliant.
她和亨特的整场对手戏都太精彩了。

1155
00:50:21.110 --> 00:50:23.610
She's like, good luck with the band.
她对他说，祝你的乐队好运。

1156
00:50:24.030 --> 00:50:25.930
Don't let them change you here.
别让他们在这里改变你。

1157
00:50:26.250 --> 00:50:27.450
It's so good.
真是太棒了。

1158
00:50:28.310 --> 00:50:31.410
Well, she drops a bunch of her stuff on the ground.
接着，她把一大堆东西掉在了地上。

1159
00:50:31.410 --> 00:50:34.450
And Hunter and Michael are trying to help her pick it up.
亨特和迈克尔试图帮她捡起来。

1160
00:50:34.590 --> 00:50:37.250
And Lady, did you know that was not supposed to happen?
天哪，你知道这不是剧本安排的吗？

1161
00:50:37.530 --> 00:50:38.590
I did know that.
我知道。

1162
00:50:38.590 --> 00:50:41.490
I did know that because they talked about it in the DVD commentary.
我知道是因为他们在DVD评论音轨里聊过这个。

1163
00:50:42.070 --> 00:50:46.650
Melora said she had this box full of like what was Jan's belongings, right?
梅洛拉说她拿了个箱子，里面装的好像是简的私人物品，对吧？

1164
00:50:46.850 --> 00:50:49.730
And it was sort of an awkward, different shaped iteMs.
那是一种有点尴尬、形状各异的物品。

1165
00:50:49.730 --> 00:50:51.830
And a few things spilled out.
然后有些东西洒了出来。

1166
00:50:51.830 --> 00:50:53.930
And Ken did not yell cut.
肯（导演）并没有喊停。

1167
00:50:54.170 --> 00:50:55.910
He just let the scene play out.
他只是让这场戏继续演下去。

1168
00:50:56.070 --> 00:50:58.430
And Michael and Hunter, everyone just stayed in the moment.
迈克尔、亨特以及每个人都完全沉浸在情境中。

1169
00:50:58.530 --> 00:50:59.870
They're trying to help her put things back.
他们试着帮她把东西装回去。

1170
00:51:00.010 --> 00:51:02.950
And Melora said they actually had a hard time getting everything to fit back in.
梅洛拉说，实际上他们很难把所有东西都塞回箱子里。

1171
00:51:03.090 --> 00:51:05.290
And that's why that played out so long.
这就是为什么那一幕持续了那么久。

1172
00:51:05.410 --> 00:51:08.150
But everyone's reactions are perfect.
但每个人的反应都完美极了。

1173
00:51:08.350 --> 00:51:09.410
David's like, what's happening?
大卫的表情就像是在问，发生什么事了？

1174
00:51:09.630 --> 00:51:11.350
And then you have Jim and Karen.
然后你看看吉姆和凯伦。

1175
00:51:11.770 --> 00:51:14.070
That was all unscripted.
那全都是即兴发挥的。

1176
00:51:15.170 --> 00:51:17.030
I love stuff like that.
我就喜欢这种桥段。

1177
00:51:17.190 --> 00:51:18.010
I love that.
我太喜欢了。

1178
00:51:18.130 --> 00:51:23.450
And, you know, it reminds me, Angela, when I've had to do scenes where I have to carry a lot of stuff.
你知道的，安吉拉，这让我想起我以前拍戏时也得拿一大堆东西。

1179
00:51:23.970 --> 00:51:31.550
A lot of times they'll give you like a suitcase that's empty or they'll give you a bag and it doesn't really have much in it.
很多时候剧组会给你一个空行李箱，或者给你一个里面没多少东西的包。

1180
00:51:31.550 --> 00:51:36.670
And I had to shoot this scene where I was coming through the door and I had all this junk.
我曾拍过一场戏，我要推门进来，手里拿了一大堆杂物。

1181
00:51:36.910 --> 00:51:39.210
And I said, will you make it real?
我说，你们能把它弄得真实一点吗？

1182
00:51:39.510 --> 00:51:39.850
Yeah.
对。

1183
00:51:40.030 --> 00:51:47.510
Because I think that if I'm really struggling with it, if I'm not pretending to struggle with it, it'll just be better.
因为我觉得如果我是真的在费劲拿，而不是假装吃力，效果会更好。

1184
00:51:47.730 --> 00:51:53.610
And I swear every time I would do the scene, some other insane thing would happen.
我发誓，每次我演这场戏时，总会发生一些意想不到的疯狂状况。

1185
00:51:53.750 --> 00:51:57.110
And it was so much better than if I was faking it.
这比我假装出来的效果好太多了。

1186
00:51:57.310 --> 00:51:57.390
Yeah.
对啊。

1187
00:51:57.670 --> 00:51:59.770
And so because these are the moments, right?
因为这就是那些精彩瞬间，对吧？

1188
00:51:59.770 --> 00:52:02.770
This was a real life moment and everyone rolled with it.
这是一个真实发生的瞬间，大家都随机应变了下来。

1189
00:52:02.870 --> 00:52:05.130
And it was so funny.
而且真的太搞笑了。

1190
00:52:05.450 --> 00:52:06.590
It's so funny.
太逗了。

1191
00:52:06.710 --> 00:52:07.490
But you're right.
不过你说得对。

1192
00:52:07.750 --> 00:52:12.010
Those real moments that the camera captures when we're playing make-believe.
当我们在假装演戏时，镜头捕捉到的正是这些真实的瞬间。

1193
00:52:12.090 --> 00:52:17.650
I always think about that famous scene on Friends where they're trying to get that sofa up the stairwell.
我总是想起《老友记》里那个著名的场景，他们想把沙发搬上楼梯间。

1194
00:52:17.870 --> 00:52:19.830
And Ross is yelling, pivot!
罗斯在大喊，旋转！

1195
00:52:20.810 --> 00:52:21.310
Pivot!
旋转！

1196
00:52:23.540 --> 00:52:24.420
Holding the sofa.
扶着沙发。

1197
00:52:24.660 --> 00:52:27.180
Like these are these moments I love because it's like real life.
我就是喜欢这些时刻，因为这就像是真实的生话。

1198
00:52:27.380 --> 00:52:29.020
But Melora did say one thing.
不过梅洛拉确实提到了一件事。

1199
00:52:29.640 --> 00:52:37.100
She said, if you notice, if you watch the scene, the whole time we're picking up items and putting them back in the box, you do not see my face.
她说，如果你注意看，仔细看这场戏，在我们捡东西并把它们放回箱子的整个过程中，你是看不到我的脸的。

1200
00:52:37.260 --> 00:52:42.920
Because I bent over as far as I could so my hair would hide my face because I am laughing so hard.
因为我把腰弯得不能再低，好让头发挡住我的脸，因为我笑得太厉害了。

1201
00:52:43.100 --> 00:52:49.910
Oh, look at that.
哦，快看那个。

1202
00:52:51.530 --> 00:52:57.890
Well, Michael then tells David, hey, just let me know about the job.
然后迈克尔对大卫说，嘿，有工作的事通知我一声就行。

1203
00:52:58.070 --> 00:52:59.170
Let me know when you know.
有消息了告诉我。

1204
00:52:59.910 --> 00:53:02.210
And David is like, you're not getting the job.
大卫的反应则是，你没得到这份工作。

1205
00:53:02.470 --> 00:53:02.630
Yeah.
是啊。

1206
00:53:03.830 --> 00:53:07.530
And so then, of course, Michael is like, I withdraw myself from consideration.
所以紧接着，理所当然地，迈克尔就说，我主动退出竞争。

1207
00:53:07.830 --> 00:53:09.470
Do you accept my withdrawal?
你接受我的退出吗？

1208
00:53:09.830 --> 00:53:11.050
David's like, yeah.
大卫说，接受。

1209
00:53:13.110 --> 00:53:14.310
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1210
00:53:15.170 --> 00:53:15.970
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1211
00:53:16.390 --> 00:53:20.370
And then Michael's like, but do I get to keep my job at Scranton?
然后迈克尔又说，那我还能保住斯克兰顿的工作吗？

1212
00:53:20.630 --> 00:53:21.710
And David's like, yes.
大卫说，可以。

1213
00:53:21.810 --> 00:53:23.790
And he goes, good, because that's all I ever really wanted.
他说，太好了，因为这本来就是我唯一真正想要的东西。

1214
00:53:25.350 --> 00:53:31.450
Well, speaking of Scranton, Michael's going to be in for a surprise.
好了，说到斯克兰顿，迈克尔要大吃一惊了。

1215
00:53:31.450 --> 00:53:41.150
Because Andy and Dwight are painting Dwight's new office, Michael's old office, soon to be office again, black.
因为安迪和德怀特正在把德怀特的新办公室——也就是迈克尔的旧办公室、很快又要变成他办公室的地方——漆成黑色。

1216
00:53:41.570 --> 00:53:43.510
They're painting all the walls black.
他们把所有的墙都漆成黑色。

1217
00:53:43.810 --> 00:53:55.810
Well, Michael's going to be really surprised because he also, in a deleted scene, told Dwight, don't do anything to my office for one month out of sort of like mourning.
好吧，迈克尔会大吃一惊，因为他在一个被删减的片段里还告诉过德怀特，出于某种哀悼，一个月内不要对我的办公室做任何改动。

1218
00:53:56.310 --> 00:54:00.890
Like, don't touch anything for one month to honor my absence.
就像是，一个月内什么都别动，以纪念我的离去。

1219
00:54:02.250 --> 00:54:04.650
And Dwight immediately starts painting it black.
而德怀特一转身就开始刷黑漆了。

1220
00:54:05.370 --> 00:54:07.990
We had a lot of questions about how we did this.
我们收到了很多关于我们是怎么做到这一点的提问。

1221
00:54:08.730 --> 00:54:10.450
They did not paint the real walls.
他们并没有粉刷真正的墙壁。

1222
00:54:10.770 --> 00:54:14.510
They brought in other fake walls that were black.
他们搬来了其他黑色的假墙。

1223
00:54:14.710 --> 00:54:14.970
Yeah.
对。

1224
00:54:15.170 --> 00:54:18.090
So we did not paint the walls that were Michael's office.
所以我们并没有粉刷迈克尔办公室原本的墙。

1225
00:54:18.370 --> 00:54:19.970
They made dummy walls.
他们做了替代用的假墙。

1226
00:54:20.170 --> 00:54:21.330
And then they could take them down.
然后他们可以把这些假墙拆下来。

1227
00:54:21.810 --> 00:54:22.250
Yes.
对的。

1228
00:54:22.350 --> 00:54:23.770
And the old walls were right behind.
而真正的旧墙就在后面。

1229
00:54:24.190 --> 00:54:25.230
Yes, very easily.
对，非常轻松。

1230
00:54:25.370 --> 00:54:26.410
But they were really painting.
不过他们确实是在粉刷。

1231
00:54:26.470 --> 00:54:26.910
Yeah.
对。

1232
00:54:26.910 --> 00:54:32.210
And they had different panels of these fake walls that they would paint throughout this scene.
而且他们在这场戏中准备了不同板块的假墙供他们粉刷。

1233
00:54:32.510 --> 00:54:38.190
But, yeah, it was very easy to reset it back to the original Michael's office.
不过，是的，要把它恢复成迈克尔原本的办公室非常简单。

1234
00:54:38.890 --> 00:54:46.150
Well, Jenna, back in New York, one of the things we didn't talk about was Jim and Karen's reaction to Jan's big meltdown.
珍娜，回到纽约，我们有一件事没聊到，那就是吉姆和凯伦对简情绪大崩溃的反应。

1235
00:54:46.370 --> 00:54:49.810
I mean, Karen's like, wow, that was really self-destructive.
我是说，凯伦的反应是，哇，那真的太自我毁灭了。

1236
00:54:49.810 --> 00:54:52.970
And Jim is like, I kind of feel bad for her.
而吉姆则说，我有点同情她。

1237
00:54:54.250 --> 00:54:56.190
Yeah, Karen does not feel bad for her.
没错，凯伦可一点都不同情她。

1238
00:54:57.130 --> 00:54:57.430
Yeah.
是啊。

1239
00:54:57.690 --> 00:54:59.850
Karen's like, I don't know.
凯伦觉得，我不知道。

1240
00:55:00.030 --> 00:55:04.050
I think she's not having any sympathy for Jan.
我觉得她对简一点同情心都没有。

1241
00:55:04.370 --> 00:55:04.670
No.
没有。

1242
00:55:05.150 --> 00:55:06.230
Karen is done.
凯伦已经受够了。

1243
00:55:07.010 --> 00:55:08.810
She is done with these folks.
她受够这群人了。

1244
00:55:09.770 --> 00:55:13.590
Well, speaking of done, Jim still has to go into his interview.
好吧，说到受够了，吉姆还得去参加面试。

1245
00:55:13.930 --> 00:55:15.570
And I thought this was interesting.
我觉得这挺有意思的。

1246
00:55:16.790 --> 00:55:21.610
Jim was like, hey, you know, if you want to take off, I can just, you know, meet you later.
吉姆说，嘿，你知道的，如果你想先走，我可以，你知道的，待会儿再碰头。

1247
00:55:21.830 --> 00:55:23.330
And Karen kind of jumps on it.
凯伦顺水推舟地抓住了这个机会。

1248
00:55:23.430 --> 00:55:26.170
She's like, yeah, actually, I wanted to meet some friends downtown for lunch.
她说，好啊，其实我本来就想去市中心找几个朋友吃午饭。

1249
00:55:26.330 --> 00:55:26.650
Do you mind?
你介意吗？

1250
00:55:26.850 --> 00:55:27.010
Bye.
拜拜。

1251
00:55:28.130 --> 00:55:31.730
Now, I didn't see that as, like, weird.
我觉得这其实并不怎么奇怪。

1252
00:55:31.730 --> 00:55:36.430
That seemed like, you know, if she's just sitting in a lobby just waiting for him and
