01:01:59.830 --> 01:02:03.910
David Wallace should have started the interview by saying, will you be my best friend?
大卫·华莱士一开场就该说，你愿意做我的好朋友吗？

1411
01:02:04.510 --> 01:02:05.510
It's so true.
太对了。

1412
01:02:06.190 --> 01:02:07.890
Everybody wants Jim to be their best friend.
每个人都想让吉姆做他们的好朋友。

1413
01:02:08.990 --> 01:02:10.610
He's a very likable guy.
他是个很讨人喜欢的人。

1414
01:02:10.890 --> 01:02:10.970
He's a good best friend.
他是个很好的好朋友。

1415
01:02:11.290 --> 01:02:11.650
Yeah.
是啊。

1416
01:02:11.910 --> 01:02:12.950
He's a great guy.
他是个极好的人。

1417
01:02:13.130 --> 01:02:13.330
Yeah.
是啊。

1418
01:02:13.330 --> 01:02:17.970
So David's asking him a few questions and he says, what is your favorite thing?
所以大卫问了他几个问题，然后问，你最喜欢的是什么？

1419
01:02:18.070 --> 01:02:20.190
What do you like most about the Scranton office?
你最喜欢斯克兰顿办公室的什么？

1420
01:02:21.230 --> 01:02:28.730
And it's right at this moment that Jim opens up his little folder and there is like a note
就在这个时候，吉姆打开他的小文件夹，里面有一张

1421
01:02:28.730 --> 01:02:36.010
of encouragement from Pam along with a little yogurt lid that she has saved since Office
潘的鼓励便条，还有一个她从办公室奥运会

1422
01:02:36.010 --> 01:02:36.650
Olympics.
一直留到现在的酸奶盖。

1423
01:02:37.210 --> 01:02:39.030
You know what that note says to me?
你知道那张便条对我说的是什么吗？

1424
01:02:39.730 --> 01:02:40.330
What?
什么？

1425
01:02:40.330 --> 01:02:43.310
I would have waited for you until after your interview.
我本会一直等你到面试结束。

1426
01:02:45.930 --> 01:02:50.090
I wouldn't have gone and met my friends for a boozy lunch somewhere.
我才不会跑去跟朋友在什么地方吃喝到酩酊大醉呢。

1427
01:02:51.010 --> 01:02:51.470
Exactly.
一点没错。

1428
01:02:52.110 --> 01:02:53.410
Thank you, Angela.
谢谢你，安吉拉。

1429
01:02:53.570 --> 01:02:53.990
Thank you.
谢谢。

1430
01:02:54.170 --> 01:02:54.650
You matter.
你很重要。

1431
01:02:54.670 --> 01:02:56.670
And what happens to you matters to me.
而你的事对我来说也很重要。

1432
01:02:57.510 --> 01:02:57.710
Yeah.
是啊。

1433
01:02:59.670 --> 01:03:06.310
And Jim looks at that and he says his favorite thing about the Scranton office were the friendships.
然后吉姆看了看那个，说他最喜欢斯克兰顿办公室的是那些友谊。

1434
01:03:07.870 --> 01:03:11.430
And that's when David asks him, where do you see yourself in 10 years?
就在那时大卫问他，你觉得十年后的自己在哪里？

1435
01:03:11.770 --> 01:03:13.230
Well, Jim is rattled now.
好吧，吉姆现在慌神了。

1436
01:03:13.430 --> 01:03:15.690
He had all these answers ready to go.
他本来把所有答案都准备好了。

1437
01:03:15.690 --> 01:03:21.370
So I'm sure he had prepared for this interview, but now Pam is there with him.
所以我敢肯定他为这次面试做了准备，但现在潘和他在一起。

1438
01:03:22.670 --> 01:03:22.850
Yeah.
是啊。

1439
01:03:23.090 --> 01:03:24.850
And we flash back to the beach.
然后我们闪回到海滩。

1440
01:03:25.950 --> 01:03:29.450
And we hear Jim tells Pam why he left Scranton.
我们听到吉姆告诉潘他为什么离开斯克兰顿。

1441
01:03:29.810 --> 01:03:32.790
He acknowledges he's never really come back.
他承认自己从来没有真正回来过。

1442
01:03:32.990 --> 01:03:36.150
And then Pam, talk about some Pam sass.
然后是潘，真是有够辣的。

1443
01:03:36.330 --> 01:03:38.130
I thought this was super ballsy.
我觉得这太有种了。

1444
01:03:38.130 --> 01:03:40.170
She's like, well, I wish you would.
她说，嗯，我希望你回来。

1445
01:03:40.830 --> 01:03:41.750
Woo-hoo-hoo!
呜呼！

1446
01:03:42.250 --> 01:03:42.590
Yeah.
是啊。

1447
01:03:42.810 --> 01:03:47.210
Well, now we sort of hear Jim's interview.
好了，现在我们算是听到吉姆的面试了。

1448
01:03:47.510 --> 01:03:51.050
We hear like he's distracted.
我们听到他好像分心了。

1449
01:03:51.050 --> 01:03:52.510
He's making jokes.
他在开玩笑。

1450
01:03:52.510 --> 01:04:00.210
We cut to a Pam talking head where she explains she hasn't really heard anything.
镜头切到一个潘的单人采访画面，她解释说她其实没听到什么消息。

1451
01:04:01.050 --> 01:04:02.950
Jim probably got the job.
吉姆可能得到这份工作了。

1452
01:04:03.190 --> 01:04:05.730
You know, there's no reason for him not to get the job.
你知道的，他没有任何理由拿不到这份工作。

1453
01:04:07.450 --> 01:04:13.950
And she's really like, you can see her trying to process it and stay really positive.
而她真的很像那种，你能看出她在努力消化这一切，并且努力保持乐观。

1454
01:04:13.950 --> 01:04:23.070
She's all day, she's been trying to stay really positive about this and convincing herself that her and Jim are friends.
她整整一天都在努力对此保持乐观，说服自己她和吉姆是朋友。

1455
01:04:23.130 --> 01:04:24.510
This is in the paSt.
这已经过去了。

1456
01:04:24.690 --> 01:04:26.090
The beach was just closure.
去海滩只是一次了断。

1457
01:04:26.310 --> 01:04:27.650
That was closure.
那是一个了断。

1458
01:04:28.370 --> 01:04:33.930
And, you know, she says, we just never got the timing right.
而且，你知道，她说，我们只是时机总是不对。

1459
01:04:34.090 --> 01:04:35.290
And that's okay.
没关系。

1460
01:04:35.630 --> 01:04:37.230
And then Jim walks in the room.
然后吉姆走进了房间。

1461
01:04:37.590 --> 01:04:40.430
I mean, she's so surprised to see him.
我的意思是，她看到他太惊讶了。

1462
01:04:40.430 --> 01:04:45.770
Yeah, he interrupts the talking head and asks her if she wants to have dinner.
对，他打断了单人采访，问她想不想一起吃晚餐。

1463
01:04:45.950 --> 01:04:47.070
She says, yeah.
她说，好啊。

1464
01:04:47.290 --> 01:04:48.990
And then he's like, it's a date.
然后他说，那就这么定咯。

1465
01:04:49.730 --> 01:04:53.950
Jenna, many, many people have talked about how great you are in that moment.
珍娜，有好多好多人都谈过你在那一刻的表现有多棒。

1466
01:04:53.970 --> 01:04:54.910
And you are.
而你也确实很棒。

1467
01:04:55.070 --> 01:04:55.730
You are.
真的很棒。

1468
01:04:55.870 --> 01:04:58.050
You are so good in that moment.
你在那一刻表现得太出色了。

1469
01:04:58.310 --> 01:05:02.030
So many emotions go across your face and your eyes tear up.
各种情绪掠过你的脸庞，你的眼泪夺眶而出。

1470
01:05:02.410 --> 01:05:03.890
Ken Kuapis said you made him cry.
肯·夸皮斯说你把他弄哭了。

1471
01:05:04.090 --> 01:05:05.250
Well, here's the thing.
好吧，情况是这样的。

1472
01:05:06.090 --> 01:05:09.310
I owe that moment to Ken Kuapis.
我把那一刻归功于肯·夸皮斯。

1473
01:05:09.310 --> 01:05:10.970
And I'll tell you why.
我会告诉你为什么。

1474
01:05:11.150 --> 01:05:17.350
A lot of people wrote in and wanted to know what was going through my head during that scene when Jim finally asked Pam out.
很多人写信来，想知道当吉姆终于约潘时，我脑子里在想什么。

1475
01:05:19.720 --> 01:05:27.620
It's crazy because Ken Kuapis, he was a type of father figure to us, right, Angela?
这太疯狂了，因为肯·夸皮斯，他就像是我们的父亲一样，对吧，安吉拉？

1476
01:05:27.780 --> 01:05:33.400
When he was on the podcast, he explained that his technique is to love people into their best work.
他上播客时解释过，他的技巧是用爱来激发人们的最佳状态。

1477
01:05:33.600 --> 01:05:36.540
He's just a very gentle, kind soul.
他是一个非常温和、善良的人。

1478
01:05:36.760 --> 01:05:38.640
He's so, so kind.
他真的是太善良了。

1479
01:05:39.460 --> 01:05:41.580
I'm going to cry just thinking about it.
我光是想想都要哭了。

1480
01:05:41.720 --> 01:05:46.620
I think, and I don't know, but I think we got that on the first take.
我觉得，我也不太确定，但我觉得我们一条就过了。

1481
01:05:46.800 --> 01:05:49.340
I think what you are watching is the first take.
我觉得你们现在看到的这就是第一条。

1482
01:05:49.500 --> 01:05:50.040
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

1483
01:05:50.040 --> 01:05:57.700
Because we had kind of planned it out with the camera when it was going to swish over and when it was going to come back to me.
因为我们之前和摄影师规划好了，镜头什么时候摇过去，什么时候摇回来对着我。

1484
01:05:57.900 --> 01:06:06.560
So in that moment when the camera swishes back to me, I was actually looking at Ken Kuapis, and he had tears in his eyes.
所以在镜头摇回我的那一刻，我实际上是在看着肯·夸皮斯，他当时眼里含着泪水。

1485
01:06:06.560 --> 01:06:08.680
And that made me tear up.
这让我忍不住落泪了。

1486
01:06:08.800 --> 01:06:15.420
And we just shared this moment, this private moment of acknowledgement for this journey of this character.
我们只是分享了这样一个时刻，一个属于这个角色的心路历程的、充满感激的私密时刻。

1487
01:06:15.580 --> 01:06:21.400
And he smiled at me in a way that a parent smiles at you when they're proud of you.
他对我微笑的那种眼神，就像父母为你骄傲时的眼神一样。

1488
01:06:21.860 --> 01:06:27.620
Listen, if Ken Kuapis looked at me with tears in his eyes, smiling, I would disintegrate.
听着，如果肯·夸皮斯含着泪水、带着微笑看着我，我会直接融化的。

1489
01:06:27.720 --> 01:06:31.140
Because he's just, it's like your dad looking at you like that.
因为他给人的感觉，就像你爸爸那样看着你。

1490
01:06:31.540 --> 01:06:31.980
Yes.
没错。

1491
01:06:32.200 --> 01:06:32.620
Yes.
没错。

1492
01:06:32.800 --> 01:06:33.820
Like, you did it, kiddo.
就像在说，你做到了，孩子。

1493
01:06:33.960 --> 01:06:34.480
You did it.
你做到了。

1494
01:06:34.580 --> 01:06:35.020
Yes.
是的。

1495
01:06:35.680 --> 01:06:36.120
Yes.
是的。

1496
01:06:38.300 --> 01:06:44.280
And I don't even know if that performance could have been there with any other director.
我甚至不知道换作任何其他导演，还能不能呈现出那种表演。

1497
01:06:44.500 --> 01:06:45.640
Oh, I don't think so.
噢，我觉得不可能。

1498
01:06:45.840 --> 01:06:46.560
I mean, as much as...
我的意思是，不管怎么说……

1499
01:06:46.560 --> 01:06:47.820
That was a moment between Ken and I.
那是我和肯之间的一个时刻。

1500
01:06:47.920 --> 01:06:53.760
That was about so much about my personal Jenna journey with Ken Kuapis on this show.
那在很大程度上关乎我个人珍娜与肯·夸皮斯在这部剧中的心路历程。

1501
01:06:53.900 --> 01:06:56.000
From the very first day.
从第一天起就是这样。

1502
01:06:56.420 --> 01:06:56.820
Yeah.
是啊。

1503
01:06:57.100 --> 01:06:59.300
Well, it was a beautiful, beautiful moment.
那真是一个美妙绝伦的时刻。

1504
01:06:59.460 --> 01:07:04.020
And I have one question for you and all the fans out there.
我有一个问题想问你和所有的粉丝。

1505
01:07:04.760 --> 01:07:05.320
What?
什么？

1506
01:07:06.120 --> 01:07:09.600
Did Jim frickin' leave Karen in New York?
吉姆这混蛋把凯伦留在纽约了吗？

1507
01:07:10.220 --> 01:07:11.860
They rode together.
他们是一起去的。

1508
01:07:12.140 --> 01:07:13.840
He drove back alone.
但他一个人开车回来了。

1509
01:07:14.180 --> 01:07:15.400
What the F?
搞什么鬼？

1510
01:07:15.740 --> 01:07:17.000
Well, I'll tell you.
好吧，我来告诉你。

1511
01:07:17.880 --> 01:07:26.340
So, first of all, there were actually two versions in the script for the ending of this episode.
首先，其实这集的结尾剧本里有两个版本。

1512
01:07:26.520 --> 01:07:30.360
There was this version with Jim interrupting my talking head.
其中一个版本是吉姆打断了我的采访镜头。

1513
01:07:30.440 --> 01:07:33.400
And then there was a second version, which we shot.
然后我们还拍了第二个版本。

1514
01:07:33.400 --> 01:07:36.720
And in the script, it says, shoot both versions.
剧本上写着，两个版本都要拍。

1515
01:07:37.020 --> 01:07:38.400
It's not in the deleted scenes.
它不在删减片段里。

1516
01:07:38.400 --> 01:07:39.040
What is it?
那是什么？

1517
01:07:39.800 --> 01:07:40.180
Okay.
好吧。

1518
01:07:40.180 --> 01:07:42.240
It's not in the deleted scenes, but we shot it.
它不在删减片段里，但我们拍了。

1519
01:07:42.400 --> 01:07:48.540
So, in the second version, you hear voiceover of Jim throwing his interview with David.
在第二个版本里，你能听到吉姆在和大卫面试时的画外音。

1520
01:07:48.540 --> 01:07:50.660
But it's even more.
而且更过分。

1521
01:07:50.820 --> 01:07:53.340
It's like he's really cracking jokes.
就像他在开各种玩笑一样。

1522
01:07:53.520 --> 01:07:58.320
He's not taking it seriously at all to the point that David actually says, do you even
他一点都不认真，甚至让大卫直接问出

1523
01:07:58.320 --> 01:07:59.200
want this job?
你到底想不想要这份工作？

1524
01:07:59.460 --> 01:08:01.100
Oh, that would have made me uncomfortable.
哦，那会让我觉得很不自在。

1525
01:08:01.840 --> 01:08:02.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1526
01:08:02.120 --> 01:08:05.280
It really tips it a little bit more than what you see.
比起你现在看到的，那个版本把天平拨得更倾斜了一些。

1527
01:08:05.280 --> 01:08:09.220
Meanwhile, while all that's happening, you see Pam leaving for the day.
与此同时，就在这一切发生的时候，你看到潘准备下班离开。

1528
01:08:09.940 --> 01:08:11.680
She doesn't do a talking head.
她没有做采访镜头。

1529
01:08:11.900 --> 01:08:13.140
She's just leaving for the day.
她只是准备下班。

1530
01:08:13.400 --> 01:08:14.540
She gets in the elevator.
她走进了电梯。

1531
01:08:14.780 --> 01:08:16.520
She goes down the elevator.
她坐电梯下楼。

1532
01:08:16.760 --> 01:08:20.360
And then when the elevator doors open, Jim is standing there.
然后当电梯门打开时，吉姆正站在外面。

1533
01:08:21.000 --> 01:08:23.780
And she says, you're back.
潘说，你回来了。

1534
01:08:24.360 --> 01:08:27.600
And he says, yeah, do you want to go to dinner?
吉姆说，对啊，你想去吃晚饭吗？

1535
01:08:28.740 --> 01:08:31.920
And Pam says, yeah, I do.
潘说，好啊，我想去。

1536
01:08:32.340 --> 01:08:34.180
And she walks out of the elevator.
然后她走出了电梯。

1537
01:08:34.500 --> 01:08:37.360
And Jim pushes the camera back into the elevator.
吉姆把摄像机挡回了电梯里。

1538
01:08:37.360 --> 01:08:41.160
And as the doors are closing, they walk off together.
在电梯门关上的时候，他们一起走开了。

1539
01:08:41.440 --> 01:08:43.280
And he puts his arm around her.
他把胳膊搂在她肩上。

1540
01:08:43.400 --> 01:08:44.700
And they smile at each other.
他们相视一笑。

1541
01:08:44.880 --> 01:08:47.580
Oh, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.
哦，不，不，不，不，不，不，不，不，不。

1542
01:08:47.580 --> 01:08:48.660
I don't like it.
我不喜欢这样。

1543
01:08:48.760 --> 01:08:49.480
I don't like it.
我真的不喜欢。

1544
01:08:49.560 --> 01:08:50.800
I like the way it is.
我还是喜欢现在播出的这个版本。

1545
01:08:50.800 --> 01:08:56.840
Well, I touched base with Dave Rogers, who said that that scene exists, that alternate.
我跟戴夫·罗杰斯确认过了，他说那个备用场景确实存在。

1546
01:08:56.900 --> 01:08:59.240
He's like, I have that in an archive.
他说，我把那个存在档案里呢。

1547
01:08:59.780 --> 01:09:02.320
He's like, I think we should throw that up sometime.
他说，我觉得我们改天应该把它放出来看看。

1548
01:09:02.320 --> 01:09:03.780
You could see it if you want.
如果你想看的话，是可以看到的。

1549
01:09:03.900 --> 01:09:07.960
But he also said that it was never, ever part of the cut of the show.
但他也说过，它从来、从来都不是正片剪辑的一部分。

1550
01:09:08.080 --> 01:09:10.380
They always had the one in that you see now.
他们一直用的都是你现在看到的那个版本。

1551
01:09:10.480 --> 01:09:12.800
And then they would play the alternate for people.
然后他们会向大家播放备选结局。

1552
01:09:13.420 --> 01:09:15.300
Everyone voted for what you see.
所有人都投票选了你现在看到的这个。

1553
01:09:16.520 --> 01:09:27.320
But they also shot in New York an ending where you see Karen crying because Jim broke up with her.
但他们在纽约还拍了一个结局，你会看到卡伦在哭，因为吉姆和她分手了。

1554
01:09:27.800 --> 01:09:29.680
And I'm sure Dave Rogers has that.
我敢肯定戴夫·罗杰斯有那个片段。

1555
01:09:29.900 --> 01:09:33.440
I picture Dave Rogers having this hard drive in a vault.
我脑补戴夫·罗杰斯把这个硬盘锁在保险库里。

1556
01:09:33.580 --> 01:09:34.700
And it's like Mission Impossible.
就像《碟中谍》一样。

1557
01:09:34.900 --> 01:09:37.300
It's like ding, ding, ding, ding, ding, ding, ding.
就像叮、叮、叮、叮、叮、叮、叮。

1558
01:09:38.600 --> 01:09:46.300
And with all these codes and traps because he is holding on to some serious office footage.
周围布满了各种密码和陷阱，因为他手里握着一些不得了的办公室素材。

1559
01:09:46.620 --> 01:09:51.160
Well, listen, now we find out who does get the job.
好吧，听着，现在我们知道了到底是谁得到了这份工作。

1560
01:09:51.340 --> 01:09:52.460
We know it's not Jim.
我们知道不是吉姆。

1561
01:09:52.680 --> 01:09:53.800
We know it's not Michael.
我们知道不是迈克尔。

1562
01:09:54.140 --> 01:09:56.100
We're assuming it's Karen.
我们原本以为是卡伦。

1563
01:09:56.280 --> 01:09:57.340
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

1564
01:09:57.520 --> 01:09:59.680
Someone else interviewed and they had an MBA.
还有别人去面试了，而且他有MBA学位。

1565
01:10:01.200 --> 01:10:04.020
Yes, an unknown MBA.
没错，一个未知的MBA。

1566
01:10:04.460 --> 01:10:06.880
Masters of Business Administration.
工商管理硕士。

1567
01:10:07.440 --> 01:10:08.240
Is that right?
是这样吗？

1568
01:10:09.080 --> 01:10:09.840
Don't know.
不知道。

1569
01:10:10.640 --> 01:10:11.520
Not sure.
不确定。

1570
01:10:12.200 --> 01:10:14.180
Masters of Business something with an A.
反正就是工商管理什么什么的，带个A字。

1571
01:10:16.140 --> 01:10:17.760
Guys, it's Ryan.
伙计们，是瑞安。

1572
01:10:18.540 --> 01:10:21.980
Ryan the temp will not be getting your coffee anymore.
临时工瑞安再也不会帮你们买咖啡了。

1573
01:10:22.440 --> 01:10:23.900
He's going to corporate.
他要去总公司了。

1574
01:10:24.180 --> 01:10:28.300
Well, we talked about this last week with Paul because a lot of people wanted to know,
嗯，我们上周跟保罗聊过这个，因为很多人想知道，

1575
01:10:28.480 --> 01:10:30.260
why does Ryan get the job?
为什么瑞安能得到这份工作？

1576
01:10:30.420 --> 01:10:37.000
And you know, lady, Dave Rogers told me they did shoot an alternate scene where Karen gets the job.
你知道吗，女士，戴夫·罗杰斯告诉我，他们确实拍了一个卡伦得到工作的备选场景。

1577
01:10:38.020 --> 01:10:42.780
Where she's crying in New York and then the phone rings and they offer her the job.
在那里她在纽约哭泣，然后电话铃响了，他们录用了她。

1578
01:10:42.920 --> 01:10:48.960
So I just think it's very, very interesting how they left options on the table for this big finale.
所以我只是觉得，他们为了这个宏大的大结局留下了这么多备选方案，真的非常非常有趣。

1579
01:10:48.960 --> 01:10:54.680
I think maybe in some cases, they were still debating who gets the job.
我觉得也许在某些情况下，他们还在争论到底谁该得到这份工作。

1580
01:10:54.900 --> 01:10:56.540
How do Jim and Pam get together?
吉姆和帕姆是怎么走到一起的？

1581
01:10:56.880 --> 01:10:59.820
Well, yeah, it seems like they wanted to give themselves some choices.
好吧，对，看起来他们是想给自己留一些选择。

1582
01:10:59.820 --> 01:11:07.480
But we also know what was going on at this time, which is that Rashida booked her role on Parks and Rec.
但我们也知道当时发生了什么，那就是拉什达拿下了《公园与游憩》的角色。

1583
01:11:07.880 --> 01:11:09.940
And she was going to be starting that job.
她马上就要开始那份工作了。

1584
01:11:10.120 --> 01:11:17.180
So A, they needed, you know, finally Jim and Pam to be together without any kind of distraction.
所以第一，他们需要让吉姆和帕姆终于在一起，不受任何形式的干扰。

1585
01:11:17.180 --> 01:11:20.360
And also Rashida just got a great new job.
而且拉什达刚刚得到了一份很棒的新工作。

1586
01:11:20.900 --> 01:11:21.420
Yeah.
对。

1587
01:11:21.560 --> 01:11:24.600
So she can't be Michael's boss at corporate.
所以她不能去总公司当迈克尔的上司。

1588
01:11:24.800 --> 01:11:25.760
No, no.
不，不。

1589
01:11:25.760 --> 01:11:27.240
She's going to be over at Parks and Rec.
她要去《公园与游憩》那边了。

1590
01:11:27.740 --> 01:11:33.880
And I think there were a lot of story endings that had wrap-ups that didn't make it to air because it was such a big episode.
而且我觉得有很多剧情收尾因为这是一集大结局而没能播出。

1591
01:11:34.320 --> 01:11:37.960
One of them I loved was there's a scene where Jan is moving in.
我喜欢其中一个场景，简搬进来了。

1592
01:11:38.080 --> 01:11:39.020
It's moving in day.
那是搬家日。

1593
01:11:39.220 --> 01:11:40.240
There's a moving truck.
有一辆搬家卡车。

1594
01:11:40.240 --> 01:11:44.340
There's, like, guys, and she's barking orders at them in front of the condo.
有几个搬家工人在那儿，她在公寓前对他们大喊大叫、发号施令。

1595
01:11:44.440 --> 01:11:47.020
And Michael's just watching it all in horror.
而迈克尔在一旁惊恐地看着这一切。

1596
01:11:47.200 --> 01:11:48.960
He's like, oh, crap.
他心想，天哪。

1597
01:11:49.480 --> 01:11:50.920
What have I done?
我都干了些什么？

1598
01:11:50.980 --> 01:11:53.300
And it's such a good scene.
这是一个非常棒的场景。

1599
01:11:54.500 --> 01:11:55.740
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1600
01:11:56.120 --> 01:11:59.600
They had to rent that location and shoot that scene.
他们还不得不租下那个地方来拍那个场景。

1601
01:11:59.600 --> 01:12:01.540
And then it didn't even make it in the episode.
然后它甚至都没能在那一集里播出。

1602
01:12:02.320 --> 01:12:03.620
Yeah, I know.
对，我知道。

1603
01:12:03.880 --> 01:12:04.600
I know.
我知道。

1604
01:12:04.720 --> 01:12:08.960
But, boy, is it going to set up some good stuff like dinner party.
但是，天哪，这会为之后的精彩内容（比如晚宴）做铺垫。

1605
01:12:08.960 --> 01:12:10.540
Oh, yes.
哦，是的。

1606
01:12:10.740 --> 01:12:11.500
Dinner party.
晚宴。

1607
01:12:11.940 --> 01:12:13.920
I am so excited for that episode.
我太期待那一集了。

1608
01:12:14.100 --> 01:12:15.660
I'm so excited for season four.
我太期待第四季了。

1609
01:12:16.600 --> 01:12:23.520
I just watched the dinner party bloopers, and it got me so excited because we laughed our butts off.
我刚看了晚宴的NG片段，这让我兴奋不已，因为我们当时笑得前仰后合。

1610
01:12:23.680 --> 01:12:24.980
Oh, I can't wait to talk about it.
哦，我已经迫不及待想聊聊它了。

1611
01:12:25.220 --> 01:12:31.580
Well, guys, this rounds out season three, and we will see you soon with season four.
好了，各位，这就结束了第三季，我们第四季再见。

